This distribution contains original LightCone-Spec code and an auditable
patch series for SGLang. SGLang is licensed under Apache-2.0 and is not
distributed with this repository. The patches target:

  Repository: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang.git
  Upstream commit: 3312645a307453893a00778592f105581e3d1c3d
  Latest semantic patch SHA-256: fa723d63c031ce01f7354dfeda7b89dd4e7fa06d6fea0ceb81864918fdec1fde
  Expected final tree: fabb129063c36e9dde9a0d8b434df2f7a292c06d

The semantic patch changes SGLang to add strict schema-v3 preflight, focused
DFlash native-layer Full/LoRA updates, deterministic backend parameter plans,
resident optimizer choices, memory-bounded LoRA-coordinate Hedge decisions,
versioned frozen-KV lifecycle, event-fenced fixed-address publication,
memory accounting, and lower-level adaptation/evidence fields for the
Static/TTS/L0 target study and isolated OnlineSPEC comparison. It also carries
the server-provided ordered output token IDs through SGLang's official serving
benchmark adapter without retokenizing generated text, supports a caller-owned
HTTP session, and implements the content-bound begin/reset/finalize terminal
evidence hook for the limited TP1/DP1 DFlash surface. It also adds a
source-owned all-reset capability/state/receipt producer whose GPU semantics
remain explicitly PENDING and whose failures require a fresh process. The
third patch counts actual protocol connection create/close events on the
supported single-tokenizer HTTP/1.1 uvicorn paths, binds cumulative process/
generation/created/closed/current totals, and rejects scheduler counters,
headers, or caller-authored substitutes. Granian HTTP/2 and multiple-tokenizer
HTTP-process paths fail closed before this capability can be produced.
The second patch adds only CPU host observations for already committed tokens;
they are labelled `CPU_CONTRACT_ONLY`, cannot enter formal p99 authority, and
the benchmark emits null aggregate ITL statistics whenever client interval
coverage is incomplete rather than reducing a sparse subset.
Its focused protocol test loads only the patched modules and does not import
unrelated SGLang optional dependencies. The hook has no bundled
trusted hardware signer. The release verifier therefore keeps Static/TTS/L0
non-claimable and only Target-only release-supported. DSpark, EAGLE/EAGLE3,
NEXTN, and all TP2/DP2 execution fail before model loading. The patch includes
a CPU-only DSpark reconstruction/selector/loss/verification contract; it does
not include or authorize the DSpark CUDA adaptation worker.
See patches/sglang/manifest.json for the exact patch and tree identities.

The registered OnlineSPEC comparison is a clean-room implementation of online
learner equations described by:

  Paper: https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.12617v2
  Reference repository: https://github.com/ZinYY/OnlineSPEC
  Audited commit: e58f82eb3f3adca3a686211236bf4f6e9e7e3a2b

The reference repository did not contain a project-level license file at the
audited commit. Some individual files carry their own notices; no OnlineSPEC
source code or checkpoint utility is copied or distributed here. The reference
is recorded for scientific provenance only.

Models and datasets are external artifacts. They are not distributed by this
repository and remain subject to their respective licenses and terms.
